# Slice 346 (the book, colon-declares and forms-declare-or-call; the author 2026-11-10) and plan M11 5a (the author
# 2026-11-11): what declares and what writes. A place is declared by its receiver (`int: i 1`, `@: p Model`) and written
# by `:=`. A form `Name: tail` declares a Structure with the tail inside, its atoms not expanded: a path through an atom
# reaches the entity its word names -- Holder\Model is the Structure Model, one instance reached through Holder, through
# the reference p and by its own name; Pair\i is the place i, so a write through it is seen by i -- and an atom that
# names nothing stays a word (unknown_word). Declared again, Pair is one more occurrence of the name: data\[0]Pair has
# two fields, data\[1]Pair three; a bare Pair would be ambiguous.
int: i 1
i := 6
int: i2 i + 1
Model:
    int: v 1
end: Model
@: p Model
Holder: Model unknown_word
Holder\Model\v := 5
int: through_model Model\v
int: through_ref p\v
Pair: a b
int: n_first length(data\[0]Pair)
Pair: i Model later
int: n_second length(data\[1]Pair)
data\[1]Pair\i := 9
int: shared i
int: later 3
